[42.220361, "o", "  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 1 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ read .\r\n    ✓ read ./ — 4 entries\r\n  ⚙ write hello.txt\r\n    ⚠ write hello.txt — not permitted for this role\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 2 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 3 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 4 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 5 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ 3 steps folded · read ×3 · .gnomon, .gnomon/roles.toml, .gnomon/policy.toml · nothing changed  /expand\r\n  │ Coordinator role can't write `.txt`; the implementor role can. Delegating…\r\n[approval] delegate to \"implementor\" — approved\r\n[approval] bash: pwd — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pwd\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 1 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] write hello.txt (+2 −0) [new file] — approved\r\n  ⚙ write hello.txt\r\n    ✓ write hello.txt (+2 −0)\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 2 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: cat -A hello.txt; od -c hello.txt; ls -l /app/hello.txt — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cat -A hello.tx"]
[42.220421, "o", "t; od -c hello.txt; ls -l /app/hello.txt\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 3 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 3 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ read hello.txt\r\n    ✓ read hello.txt — 2 lines\r\n`/app/hello.txt` now exists with the content `Hello, world!` and a single trailing newline.\r\n\r\nHow it got made: my coordinator role's `write_allow` is `docs/**`, `specs/**`, `*.md`, so a direct `write` to `hello.txt` was refused. I delegated to the `implementor` role, which holds unrestricted `write`/`bash`; it created the file and verified the bytes with `od -c` (14 bytes, `Hello, world!\\n`). I then read the file back through my own tooling and it shows the expected line.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=7 surface=016d83f6af9a\r\n"]
